{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"ec66e52411ba563376289d729c0707d222b165e9b0fbaeb722b12c8be5b6acd1","digest":{"component_or_area":"metrics snapshot writer/reader","key_entities":["src/rebar/metrics/snapshot.py","write_snapshot()","read_snapshots()",".rebar/metrics-snapshots.ndjson",".gitignore","tests/unit/metrics/test_snapshot.py"],"problem_keywords":["metrics snapshot","ndjson","persistence","trend tracking","code health","git tracking"],"propositions":["A durable append-only NDJSON snapshot store must persist point-in-time code-health metrics (coverage, complexity, clone count) in the git-tracked .rebar/ directory so trend series accumulates across CI runs.","The snapshot writer must append timestamped records and the reader must filter by date range, returning only records within a specified since/until window.","The snapshot file path .rebar/metrics-snapshots.ndjson must be explicitly un-ignored in .gitignore via a negation rule so the metrics history persists and syncs with git.","Malformed or truncated NDJSON lines must be skipped without raising an exception, allowing the reader to return only valid records."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787359668739096001,"uuid":"a38d9915-08c3-422a-af4a-94e27f1d28cd"}